{"name":"Atoll","hex":"#2b797a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"atoll","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of island consisting of a ribbon reef that nearly or entirely surrounds a lagoon and supports, in most cases, one to many islets on the reef platform."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atoll"}],"entries":[{"title":"Atoll","blocks":[{"text":"An atoll is a ring-shaped island, including a coral rim that encircles a lagoon. There may be coral islands or cays on the rim. Atolls are located in warm tropical or subtropical parts of the oceans and seas where corals can develop. Most of the approximately 440 atolls in the world are in the Pacific Ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Tetiaroa_from_sky.JPG/330px-Tetiaroa_from_sky.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atoll","wikidata":"Q42523"},{"title":"Atoll (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Atoll is a French progressive rock band formed in Metz in 1972 and active until 1981. Different iterations of the group have since coalesced around prominent members, including Chris Beya and André Balzer."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atoll_(band)","wikidata":"Q2070724"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/On_the_structure_and_distribution_of_coral_reefs_BHL40453231.jpg/500px-On_the_structure_and_distribution_of_coral_reefs_BHL40453231.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/On_the_structure_and_distribution_of_coral_reefs_BHL40453231.jpg/1280px-On_the_structure_and_distribution_of_coral_reefs_BHL40453231.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/On_the_structure_and_distribution_of_coral_reefs_BHL40453231.jpg/500px-On_the_struc